  "result": "I fixed the odd ordering in `--help`. The names for a single option were coming out longest-prefix first, so you got `--verbose, -v` instead of `-v, --verbose`.\n\nThe cause was in `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py`. It sorted the option names with `reverse=True`, which put the longest prefix first. I removed the `reverse=True`, so short options come before long ones again.\n\nThe full test suite passes (1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed). I didn't add a test for the ordering, and nothing is committed.\n\nI didn't change the order in which separate options are listed. The code that builds that order (`get_params` in `core.py` and the decorator handling in `decorators.py`) looks fine. If your problem was options appearing in the wrong sequence rather than names within one option, tell me and I'll look at that next.",
